1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,674
A recall hits your pharmacy.

2
00:00:01,674 --> 00:00:03,348
Which patients received that lot?

3
00:00:03,348 --> 00:00:06,026
Today, in most pharmacies, nobody knows for sure.

4
00:00:06,026 --> 00:00:08,034
Someone searches paper logs, and hopes.

5
00:00:08,094 --> 00:00:14,684
Chimera Rx captures the lot at receiving, and again at fill, so the answer is already there when the recall arrives.

6
00:00:14,744 --> 00:00:20,191
Everything you will see runs on synthetic data, in a real browser, against the real application.

7
00:00:20,251 --> 00:00:22,142
Each role sees a different pharmacy.

8
00:00:22,142 --> 00:00:28,130
The technician receives a delivery: scan the GS1 DataMatrix, and the lot gate checks the transaction information and statement.

9
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:30,966
The expiry and the recall list are checked too.

10
00:00:30,966 --> 00:00:35,063
Then the stock is shelved, in the aisle and bay the app suggests.

11
00:00:35,123 --> 00:00:36,900
The pharmacist fills and verifies.

12
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,810
Rx Watcher and Rx Guardian raise suggestions, each with its evidence.

13
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:45,076
Accept one, and the order goes on hold until the pharmacist decides.

14
00:00:45,136 --> 00:00:50,579
The cashier does pickup and the front store register, but cannot see allergies, birth dates or recalls.

15
00:00:50,579 --> 00:00:52,500
The menu is short on purpose.

16
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:57,689
The admin manages partner access only, in Integrations, and cannot see patients at all.

17
00:00:57,749 --> 00:00:58,654
Now a recall.

18
00:00:58,654 --> 00:01:02,577
A fax arrives, OCR reads it, and the Coroner agent extracts the lots.

19
00:01:02,577 --> 00:01:06,500
A verbatim gate drops any lot that is not printed on the page.

20
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,210
The pharmacist confirms each lot.

21
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:13,489
Stock moves to quarantine, and the exact patients appear, matched by the lot recorded at fill.

22
00:01:13,549 --> 00:01:17,888
The messages are drafted by AI, and the pharmacist attests before anything is sent.

23
00:01:17,888 --> 00:01:19,747
They land in the sandbox outbox.

24
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:21,607
The voicemail is rendered, never dialed.

25
00:01:21,607 --> 00:01:26,565
Refills for those lots are blocked, so a recalled lot cannot go out the door again.

26
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:30,446
Agents work in the background, and every one follows the same rule.

27
00:01:30,446 --> 00:01:34,903
Rules decide, the model explains, a gate checks the model, and a pharmacist decides.

28
00:01:34,963 --> 00:01:39,848
Providers are pluggable: Bedrock, Anthropic, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a local model.

29
00:01:39,848 --> 00:01:46,768
Run Rx Guardian now, and new suggestions appear for the pharmacist, with the history behind each one.

30
00:01:46,828 --> 00:01:53,819
Partners connect through REST, an MCP server, FHIR behind OAuth, signed webhooks, and DSCSA and EPCIS exports.

31
00:01:53,819 --> 00:01:59,577
Two stores can transfer stock between them, and both audit logs record the move.

32
00:01:59,637 --> 00:02:12,739
Everything real is a designed seam: SMS, email, phone calls, wholesaler EDI, DSCSA verification, e-prescribing, the dispensing system, the EHR over FHIR, payer, secrets manager, KMS, and single sign-on.

33
00:02:12,739 --> 00:02:17,257
They are sandboxed today, and nothing reaches a real person.

34
00:02:17,317 --> 00:02:18,602
PHI fields are encrypted.

35
00:02:18,602 --> 00:02:22,458
Roles are checked on the server, not just hidden in the screen.

36
00:02:22,458 --> 00:02:25,349
The audit log is hash-chained, so an edit shows.

37
00:02:25,349 --> 00:02:28,883
An independent review found eight issues, and all eight are fixed.

38
00:02:28,883 --> 00:02:30,811
These are HIPAA-style safeguards, not certified.

39
00:02:30,871 --> 00:02:31,826
Built with Kiro.

40
00:02:31,826 --> 00:02:38,196
Specs carry requirement IDs, steering holds the safety rules, and hooks run a PHI guard and property tests on save.

41
00:02:38,196 --> 00:02:44,247
A custom agent, and a Kiro Crew team of agents, did the work, with a human reviewing every gate.

42
00:02:44,307 --> 00:02:45,592
Chimera Rx.

43
00:02:45,592 --> 00:02:48,162
github.com/pjborad/Chimera-Rx.

44
00:02:48,162 --> 00:02:50,090
Synthetic data only.

